Debug tracing for the A5 mixed-chunk FIA split.

Adds one-shot logger.info probes along the whole MIXED dispatch chain, so a
single request shows exactly how far a mixed batch gets. Every probe fires at
most once per process, so a missing line means that stage was never reached --
that is the point.

Expected sequence for one mixed batch (all seven lines, in this order):

  Scheduler.get_new_batch_prefill        "scheduler formed MIXED"
  TpModelWorker.forward_batch_generation "worker received MIXED ForwardBatch"
  PrefillCudaGraphRunner.can_run_graph   "prefill graph declines MIXED"
  ModelRunner._forward_raw               "dispatches MIXED: path=eager"
  EagerRunner._execute_extend            "EagerRunner executes MIXED"
  RadixAttention.forward                 "sees MIXED: backend=..."
  AscendAttnBackend.forward_mixed        "mixed forward: decision=split"

Two lines are failure signals, not normal output:

  "dispatches MIXED: path=prefill_graph"  -- can_run_graph() let the batch
      through; the split is about to be lost.
  "Ascend FIA BUG: a MIXED batch reached the prefill CUDA graph"  -- same
      failure, observed one layer deeper. Check that
      attn_backend.enable_fia_mixed_split is still mirrored onto whatever
      wrapper ModelRunner holds.

Apply / revert from the SGLang worktree root, not from this repo:

  cd sglang/a5_fia_mixed_split
  git apply    ../../llm/a5_fia_mixed_split_debug_logging.patch   # add prints
  git apply -R ../../llm/a5_fia_mixed_split_debug_logging.patch   # remove them

This is a debugging aid -- do not commit it to the SGLang branch. Run
`git status` before committing there. Hand-maintained against SGLang commit
1e0e0d6355; if it stops applying, re-apply what still fits, fix the rejected
hunks by hand, and regenerate with `git diff -- python/`.

